{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d9394e94f1a35e641298b412b86ca4df62a619d3","text":"Stale from birth through my own hand, and worth recording precisely because the cause was a tidying instinct.\n\nThis request rested on codex's review report cc8c8213. Minutes later I superseded artifact fc8354d5, which that review's request had cited, on the reasoning that an artifact pointing at a head with confirmed errors should not stay live. Retiring it cascaded backwards: review request 3a379ff7 went stale, then codex's promise, then their review report, and from there forward into this request, its promise, and the new artifact at the corrected head. Six live events killed by one supersession of something already answered.\n\nThe general shape: superseding a reviewed artifact retroactively invalidates the review of it and everything resting on that review. Documentation of a rejected head is not made truthful by retiring the pointer; it is made truthful by the successor artifact, which already existed. Replacement follows on a live basis."}